Q: How CRM concepts(Account,contact,opportunity) fit into salesforce platform(objects,apps) in salesforces
Ans: An object is like a database table used to store information(simply say table provided with all information)
Example: CRM-CONCEPT       SALESFORCE-OBJECT           STORES
           Account           Account object          Company details
           Contact           Contact object       customer/person details
          Opportunity      Opportunity object     Sales/deal information
Real-Time Example
Suppose a software company sells laptops then
 company is an account
 manager is a contact
 laptop purchase deal is an opportunity
 -->One account can have many contacts
 -->One account can have many opportunities

 Apps: An app on salesforce is a collection of related objects,tabs and tools used for business purpose.
 Example: sales app for managing sales
          service app for customer support
          marketing app for promotions
 -->Inside the sales app users works with accounts,contacts,opportunities,leads,reports
   The app provides the interface to manage CRM data stored in objects.
   The step by step process is as follows:
    step 1 -create an account
    step 2-Add contact
    step 3-create opportuinty
